KG42.register("clusters-cf1d36174928d2e7394de07f",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v142-d-K004","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","label":"P2P Transaction Execution and the Interface to Second-Stage Energy and Flexibility Exchange","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"P2P Transaction Execution and the Interface to Second-Stage Energy and Flexibility Exchange","market_meaning":"P2P transactions produced by the selected strategy form execution arrangements for seller injection and buyer withdrawal, and serve as existing transaction inputs for energy and flexibility exchange between prosumers and the DSO. The current chains represent only execution and participation procedures and are not yet sufficient to express complete flexibility scheduling under network constraints.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02","v141-a-M03","v141-a-M04"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","activation","participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The M04 source explicitly uses first-stage transaction outputs as second-stage inputs; sharing R009 and R014 represents two entry paths according to the selected strategy, whose results are neither added together nor identified as the same quantity. R018 retains its scope of participation permission and cannot be regarded as already representing second-stage balance merely because its source contains Eq. (28).","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is defined by the physical execution of predetermined P2P transactions and their connection to exchanges with the DSO, bringing together execution activities and second-stage participation permissions. This boundary is supported by the transaction input relationship in the source; neither the case configuration of ordinary consumers nor first-stage objectives have been incorporated into second-stage scheduling rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R016","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the seller injection and buyer withdrawal procedure for each P2P transaction."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R018","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides participation permission for prosumers to exchange energy and flexibility with the DSO, retaining its procedural formulation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Uses only the predetermined allocation and net transaction quantity under Strategy One as the source of execution inputs, without carrying the first-stage optimization objective into the second stage."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides an alternative allocation input path when Strategy Two is selected, with its results kept separate from those of Strategy One."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-NET","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e25"],"rationale":"When Strategy One is selected, predetermined bilateral transactions provide the transaction information for execution arrangements. Bilateral allocation balance is not elevated here to a physical injection equation accounting for network losses."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e25"],"rationale":"When Strategy Two is selected, its P2P allocation results enter the same execution procedure; this is a conditional input path and does not assert that the allocation quantities under the two strategies are identical."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R018","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e27"],"rationale":"The M04 source links first-stage transaction execution to the second stage, in which prosumers exchange energy and flexibility with the DSO; the two chains provide complementary procedures but do not provide the complete mathematics of balance and scheduling."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source contains the second-stage objective, energy balance, flexibility bounds, and network constraints, but the delivered M04 chains contain only execution, participation, and case configuration. R018 has no existing scientific object for Eq. (28); that equation and Eqs. (27), (29) to (43) cannot be added to the frozen catalog through D assembly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g02-e29","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e10","v141-b-g03-e11","v141-b-g03-e13","v141-b-g03-e14","v141-b-g03-e17","v141-b-g03-e18","v141-b-g03-e19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream work should establish M04 scheduling chains grounded in sources and assign the objective, balance, flexibility, and network constraints; clarify whether R018 covers only participation permission or requires an expanded scope."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"First-stage transaction quantities should serve as predetermined inputs in the second stage, but the current M04 chains have no corresponding typed objects available for mapping. Although R009 and R014 contain electricity sale quantities with the same symbol, they are decision instances of different strategies; R016 also uses power terminology, while the time scale and conversion to energy remain unspecified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R014","v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-X-P2P-NET","v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X001","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g01-en4","v141-b-g01-en5"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Specify the selected strategy, the transfer of transaction quantities, and their role as fixed second-stage inputs, and check the relationships among power, energy, and time periods; do not perform same_quantity mapping before the objects are completed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"Eq. (19) in R009 is the transaction accounting balance for bilateral allocation, while R016 is the physical injection and withdrawal procedure; network losses and nodal balance have separate second-stage sources. Equality of quantities in transaction accounts cannot directly substitute for the complete conditions of physical execution.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g03-e10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Distinguish market allocation, participant exchanges, and network physical feasibility, with upstream work specifying the scope of execution constraints; first-stage equations must not automatically be relabeled as physical lossless transmission."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"No extensions have yet been approved for flexibility commodities or services, a separate DSO role, or network constraints; the related proposals can only indicate coverage gaps and cannot merge the DSO into the LMO or flexibility into local electrical energy.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R016::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R018::V::participation.prosumer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e29","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e15","v141-b-g03-e19"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-flexibility","v141-b-g01-prop-dso","v141-b-g02-prop-flexibility-service","v141-b-g02-prop-dso-operator","v141-b-g03-p01","v141-b-g03-p02","v141-b-g03-p03"],"required_work":"Manually inspect the proposals and their definitional differences before deciding on upstream ontology extensions and chain coverage; keep all proposals pending and do not add graph objects in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The sources for execution, the second-stage interface, and the missing scheduling content are all unreviewed candidates; this cluster does not indicate that distribution network feasibility, symbol definitions, or transcription have been verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R014","v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g02-e31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually inspect the interfaces and scopes chain by chain, and independently check the second-stage and appendix content before scientific adoption."}]},"rule_refs":["10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R016","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R018","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R009","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R014"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-7b77631c556e010b","COMP-8da51d1a160b4a00","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-da34359f040da554","KG31-0645fab4a79eb10b","KG31-284fede6dbff2be2"]});
